      "repetible": "x",
      "funcion": "LOW SOFT INLAND HILLS linking the sleeping-head landscape to the aqueduct/bridges. Two overlapping low gently rolling ridge silhouettes, broad shallow valley in center to leave landmarks visible, modest more rounded hill at left and a slightly higher shoulder right. Distant pale graphite contours, very sparse fine stratum hatching and occasional tiny low ground cover, NO trees taller than a tiny shrub. No cliffs. Entire ridge belt reaches both horizontal edges at SAME elevation with matching slope for seamless repetition. Transparent sky above continuous irregular top contour, opaque light paper terrain below to bottom, no island-like cutout bottom."
    },
    {
      "archivo": "camino/18_laderas_rocosas.png",
