      "fuente": "/Users/l03123318/.codex/generated_images/01a1ae0f-3e87-7520-810d-db7f4abc5e8b/exec-b5abdc75-827a-4426-8fe7-2bc1dbb6a210.png",
      "repetible": "x",
      "funcion": "MID-DISTANCE ROCKY SLOPES linking old stone bridges to seaside lighthouse. Layered low limestone terraces and gently eroded sloping rock shelves, a broad saddle opening in middle for bridge landmark, a few fine fissures and small roots. More detailed than far hills but quieter than playable terrain. Broad landform belt spanning edge to edge, low profile not a towering mountain or cave. Same height and tangent at left/right endpoints for seamless horizontal repetition. Transparent sky above top contour, opaque warm paper land extending to bottom, no floating island lower contour."
    },
